1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:05,920
(Coming up)
Remember that day

2
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:07,040
when we climbed into the cabinet?

3
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,520
I was hiding in there alone, right?

4
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:09,600
I could hear everything.

5
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,880
Over the radio they said,
"Three, two, one, scare him!"

6
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:13,360
(Volunteering for a solo mission)
If there's an escape room today,

7
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:15,240
I'm going in first.

8
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:16,300
We'll definitely give you

9
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:17,320
(Wish granted)
plenty of room to grow.

10
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:19,200
Don't... Don't help me later, okay?

11
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:19,960
Do you know how scary

12
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:21,160
one of our solo missions was?

13
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:22,280
A little kid's voice went,

14
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:24,480
(Listening closely)
"Mommy, come find me."

15
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:25,800
"Come find me."

16
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:26,760
Then she suddenly screams,

17
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,800
"You're not my mommy!"

18
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,280
(Outsmarting the crew)
We should hint to each other.

19
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:32,080
You know, cheat a little.

20
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:34,000
That's why I said black magic.

21
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,320
How about blue? Like this?

22
00:00:35,320 --> 00:00:36,280
(Let's test it)

23
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:36,840
Blue, you know?

24
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:38,580
(Practice never hurts)
Let's drill a few.

25
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:39,680
(Addicted to the quiz)
One more.

26
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:40,840
How often does he shower?

27
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:41,880
(In unison)
- Never. - Never.

28
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:43,680
We're straight-up battling
the producers.

29
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:46,480
Don't even need to look.
I know your pick.

30
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:47,800
(Playing along)
Yeah, he has superpowers.

31
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:48,320
I have superpowers.

32
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:48,840
Really?

33
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:50,880
(Livestream rehearsal)
I only know the first line. What do I do?

34
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:51,680
It's not that strict.

35
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:54,240
That's called precise musical control.

36
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:55,720
I'm reinventing it.

37
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:56,840
All right, guys.

38
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:03,500
=Truth Clubhouse=

39
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:05,820
(Everyone's plotting something)

40
00:01:05,960 --> 00:01:06,760
Hello.

41
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:07,600
(Greetings all around)
Morning.

42
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:08,920
Looking good.

43
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:10,900
(Ding arrives)

44
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:13,060
(Ta-da! Grand entrance)

45
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:15,080
What?

46
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:16,880
You're the bad guy today, aren't you?

47
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:18,600
ESC.

48
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:19,040
Quit pretending.

49
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:19,480
Is it you?

50
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:20,040
Seriously?

51
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:21,120
(Already distracted)

52
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:22,480
You look hot.

53
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:25,720
So handsome.

54
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:26,520
So handsome!

55
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:28,200
You're definitely the bad guy today.

56
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:28,920
Definitely not.

57
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:30,640
Or maybe they just didn't show me.

58
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:31,360
What?

59
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:33,400
Maybe they just didn't show me.

60
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:35,840
The way you two are dressed today...

61
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:37,680
Are you both confirmed ESCs now?

62
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:38,640
(Not a joke to make)
Come on, don't start.

63
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:41,080
Today's theme is red vampire.

64
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:42,440
You two even have the same hair.

65
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:43,720
(Partners in crime confirmed)

66
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:44,640
Our hair does match.

67
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:45,080
Look.

68
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:46,520
Ding, we're cooked.

69
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:47,200
Yeah, we're cooked.

70
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:49,280
(Uh-oh, we're cooked)
It's our Gen Z connection.

71
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:50,480
('02-line telepathy)
You've been infected.

72
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:52,320
It's contagious.

73
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:54,160
That's our Gen Z connection.

74
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:55,840
The infected one.

75
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:56,400
One killer,

76
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:57,400
one infected.

77
00:01:58,640 --> 00:01:59,980
That's way too... one-sided.

78
00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:00,640
(Weak protest)

79
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:02,200
They know there are secret roles, right?

80
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,200
Of course.

81
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,760
The game starts in a minute.

82
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:07,040
His job is to sabotage our missions.

83
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:09,190
Whoever slacks off today is the one.

84
00:02:09,190 --> 00:02:10,190
I'm calling it now.

85
00:02:10,190 --> 00:02:11,520
Whoever doesn't try...

86
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:12,840
Remember last time,

87
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:14,600
when someone did it on purpose?

88
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:16,200
I watched that episode.

89
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,960
You and Bai, right?

90
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:19,200
Yeah, me and Bai.

91
00:02:19,780 --> 00:02:21,220
(Come on!)

92
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:22,840
Jin!

93
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:25,230
Jin!

94
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:26,560
Jin!

95
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:27,320
Do I look taller today?

96
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:29,920
Which Kardashian are you today?

97
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:31,580
(Jin Cardashian)

98
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:36,720
You're a little too hyped today.

99
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:38,040
I'm hyped again?

100
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:39,560
I'll chill for the finale, I promise.

101
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:41,000
(Jin, stay cool)
Okay.

102
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,680
Let's keep it chill this time, okay?

103
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:43,740
I just want a nice, steady life.

104
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:44,780
I'm never trusting you again.

105
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:46,500
Today, I'm not trusting anybody.

106
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:48,620
Why do you say that every day?

107
00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:50,020
Didn't you guess right yesterday?

108
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:52,500
Did I lie to you yesterday, girl?

109
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:53,540
Since day one,

110
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:55,460
I've been Nan 2.0.

111
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:57,780
(Requesting a solo mission?)

112
00:02:58,160 --> 00:02:58,880
Stare at the S.

113
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:00,960
Come on, look at that S.

114
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,080
What's it going to do?

115
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,320
We... The couch will move?

116
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:05,200
Jin, cover your legs.

117
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:05,960
Is there going to be a huge gust
of wind?

118
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:06,640
Alright, I did.

119
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:07,760
Jin, open the blanket

120
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:09,560
and cover your legs with it.

121
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:10,200
We need to keep

122
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:12,160
that floor-length-skirt look.

123
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:12,960
Long skirt?

124
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,040
(Does exactly as told)

125
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:14,920
It's not going to flip us, is it?

126
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,080
Don't worry about that yet.

127
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:17,160
Just cover up first.

128
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:18,400
No!

129
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:20,040
(I'm begging you)
I cannot handle flipping over.

130
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:21,120
Hold on.

131
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,520
(I got you, girl)
Wait, I've got tulle too.

132
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:24,040
(Slightly panicking)
Wait. Don't move.

133
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,180
Got it pinned. It's okay.

134
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:25,640
(Sweet little sis)

135
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:27,080
Okay, everyone, stare at the S.

136
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,600
What does this mean?

137
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:34,800
What's going on?

138
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:36,660
(Mechanism stops)

139
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,200
Why is it tilted?

140
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:45,180
It didn't work.

141
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:46,000
(Instantly relieved)

142
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,320
It's not going to launch us, right?

143
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:49,040
Maybe S stands for shoot.

144
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:49,600
(Wild imagination)

145
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:50,920
Shoot all six of us out?

146
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:51,560
Shoot?

147
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:53,200
No, S stands for six feet under.

148
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:54,020
(There you go again)

149
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:55,000
It stands for stupid.

150
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:56,400
(Me?)

151
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:58,760
Remember that day

152
00:03:58,760 --> 00:03:59,880
(All ears)
when we climbed into the cabinet?

153
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:01,360
I was hiding in there alone, right?

154
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,520
I could hear everything.

155
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:03,040
Over the radio they said,

156
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:04,640
"Three, two, one, scare him!"

157
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:07,760
Scare him!

158
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:09,760
(So mean!)
You guys are awful.

159
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:12,920
It's not working.

160
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:13,760
It's broken.

161
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:14,320
Broken?

162
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:15,520
Someone lied on the weight.

163
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:16,270
No idea who.

164
00:04:16,270 --> 00:04:17,510
I'm only seventy-something jin!

165
00:04:17,510 --> 00:04:18,480
(Definitely not me)
I didn't lie.

166
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:19,950
Seventy-something kilograms?

167
00:04:19,950 --> 00:04:21,270
I said seventy-something jin.

168
00:04:21,270 --> 00:04:23,000
(Misheard it completely)
Seventy-something jin.

169
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,440
We're definitely 70KG.

170
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:26,040
I'm over 80 jin myself.

171
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:28,200
Yeah, I'm seventy-something.

172
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:29,680
Everyone, give us a second.

173
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:30,280
We're rebooting it.

174
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:31,640
Just a moment.

175
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:33,000
It's fine.

176
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,200
We can just fake the flip ourselves.

177
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:35,360
That works too.

178
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:36,840
No wonder she wanted us

179
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:38,620
to wear long skirts.

180
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:41,040
Pants.

181
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:41,640
Right.

182
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:43,240
She reminded me to wear pants.

183
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,960
(Proud of myself)
Good thing I wore a long skirt.

184
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:47,360
No, I think it was meant
to lift us first.

185
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:48,440
Both sides rise together,

186
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:50,120
then it tips backward.

187
00:04:50,140 --> 00:04:51,360
(Scary just thinking about it)

188
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:52,360
They go for maximum thrills.

189
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:53,240
Didn't they say...

190
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:54,840
You can see
the track right there, right?

191
00:04:54,990 --> 00:04:56,120
Yeah, the track comes all the way here.

192
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,600
Scared?

193
00:04:58,600 --> 00:04:59,280
Nope.

194
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:01,560
If there's an escape room today,

195
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:03,000
I'm going in first.

196
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,240
You already went in first today.

197
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,840
You were brave coming in just now.

198
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:06,920
No, I mean in the dark.

199
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:07,920
If it's pitch-black, I'm going first.

200
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:08,560
Why?

201
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,920
(Setting the dark-room flag)
I really want to try it.

202
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:12,200
But when all six
of us came in just now...

203
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:14,360
Yeah, you were the one screaming.

204
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:16,200
Because it was just one dark hallway.

205
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:16,920
I can just...

206
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:17,800
Now you get it?

207
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:18,680
Now you get it, huh?

208
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,400
We'll wait for you later.

209
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:22,240
Later... Don't help me, okay?

210
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:23,360
Got it.

211
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:25,480
(Wish granted)
We'll give you plenty of room to grow.

212
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:26,660
(Maybe spoke too soon)

213
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:28,000
You can explore all by yourself.

214
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,640
We'll go in after the lights come on.

215
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:31,000
We'll all go home.

216
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:33,800
(So excited)
I think it'll be fun.

217
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,840
No solo missions these last two days.

218
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:36,480
What if there is one?

219
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,560
We'll make a solo mission just for you.

220
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:38,000
Deal?

221
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:38,960
We had one on day one.

222
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:40,520
Didn't someone hide
in the cabinet alone?

223
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:41,400
Ours was one person

224
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:42,840
walking down a hallway alone.

225
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:43,840
To grab something

226
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,000
or find something.

227
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:45,720
(Backing out already)
Then I can't do that.

228
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:46,560
Do you know how scary

229
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:47,760
one of our solo missions was?

230
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:48,880
A little kid's voice said,

231
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:51,160
(Listening closely)
"Mommy, come find me."

232
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:53,880
"Come find me."

233
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:57,000
"Mommy, go comb your hair
by the mirror."

234
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,080
Like that.

235
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:58,960
(Demo over)
Chinese-style horror?

236
00:05:58,960 --> 00:05:59,800
Yep, Chinese-style.

237
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:00,840
Then she suddenly screams,

238
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:02,640
"You're not my mommy!"

239
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:03,280
Stuff like that.

240
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:04,120
What? Say that again.

241
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,200
You're not my...

242
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:06,760
You're not my mommy.

243
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:09,080
Then she starts yelling for Dad.

244
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:11,300
(Chat time expired)

245
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:14,780
(Who's today's Game King?)

246
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:16,080
Your hair really does look alike today.

247
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,760
I mean, seriously...

248
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:19,480
But they wouldn't make it
that obvious, right?

249
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:21,660
(90% match)

250
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:23,680
Do you two have the same stylist?

251
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:24,680
Maybe.

252
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:26,520
Even your outfits are similar.

253
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:26,880
Exactly.

254
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:28,760
How'd you get those highlights in there?

255
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:30,280
They're clip-in extensions.

256
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,400
If I'm last,

257
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:35,200
you'll all look at me
like I'm stupid, right?

258
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,360
I'll secretly give you hints.

259
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:37,680
(Big sis has your back)
I'm being dumb again.

260
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:39,320
You're not dumb. You're adorable.

261
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:40,480
You're great TV, babe.

262
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:42,000
(Me?)
I'm great TV again?

263
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:42,960
Really?

264
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:43,880
Am I entertaining?

265
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:44,760
(Needs reassurance immediately)
Am I entertaining?

266
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:45,240
Yes.

267
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:45,920
Really?

268
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:46,520
(Reassurance delivered)
Very.

269
00:06:46,520 --> 00:06:47,440
You're incredible TV.

270
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:49,480
We met in the elevator on day one.

271
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:50,200
That's when we met.

272
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:50,600
I was like, today I...

273
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:51,280
Who? You and who?

274
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:52,080
Me and Ding.

275
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:53,840
I asked if I looked stupid.

276
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:54,640
He went silent.

277
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,320
Then I asked if I'd get roasted.

278
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:57,800
He said I definitely wouldn't.

279
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:59,140
That first question

280
00:06:59,140 --> 00:06:59,920
