Yeah. One each.

565
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:04,600
How come I didn't get one?

566
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:05,300
If everybody gets one, nobody gets one.

567
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:05,680
(True, though)

568
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:07,880
But Ning already broke the record.

569
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:08,720
Really?

570
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:09,720
Who broke the record?

571
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:10,920
Season 3's record

572
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:12,960
was five keys, held by Bai Yu and me.

573
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:14,920
You broke another record?

574
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:15,920
You do this every day.

575
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:17,960
Your whole career
is just breaking records.

576
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:19,800
Exactly. Everything I do

577
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:20,760
has to be a milestone.

578
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:22,520
I broke a record too, right?

579
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:23,480
What's the lowest score?

580
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:25,080
The lowest?

581
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:26,160
We're about to find out.

582
00:14:26,160 --> 00:14:27,020
(Puppy turns evil)

583
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:28,780
(I'll let you rephrase that)

584
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:29,720
Just kidding.

585
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:31,640
(Backing down)
I just like joking around.

586
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:33,120
Zhou Keyu's gone bad.

587
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:33,920
Joker.

588
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:36,840
Very funny.

589
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:38,240
So how many keys did you guys get?

590
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:38,840
Two.

591
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:40,500
(Can't keep a straight face)

592
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:44,860
(I really couldn't hold it in)

593
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,720
How do you win only two out of ten?

594
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:49,080
Three.

595
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:50,240
Three counting yesterday.

596
00:14:50,580 --> 00:14:52,720
I feel like I'm almost
trying not to win.

597
00:14:53,380 --> 00:14:54,600
(It's not like I wanted so few)

598
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:58,560
Player Ning 2K, please come in alone.

599
00:14:58,560 --> 00:15:00,280
Good luck, Ning!

600
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:02,520
Zhou Keyu...

601
00:15:02,660 --> 00:15:04,300
(Instantly turns obedient)

602
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:05,800
That actually hurts.

603
00:15:06,420 --> 00:15:08,020
(Sorry, Jin)

604
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:11,160
(Defending Ke)
We're protecting you.

605
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:12,120
Yeah, we're protecting you.

606
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:13,080
Just you wait.

607
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:14,320
That necklace

608
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:15,600
will be mine in a minute.

609
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:18,900
(Pretending I believe her)

610
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:21,960
Player Jin Pretty, come in alone.

611
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:23,400
Go. Good luck!

612
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:25,120
Know how to say no.

613
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:26,040
Say no? Got it.

614
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:26,820
(Absolutely confident)

615
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:28,680
(I'm exhausted)

616
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:30,400
And then there's black magic.

617
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:31,680
How do you play black magic?

618
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:33,040
Black magic is...

619
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:34,160
Here, I'll play a round with you.

620
00:15:34,160 --> 00:15:34,480
Okay.

621
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:35,180
Watch closely.

622
00:15:35,180 --> 00:15:35,900
(I'll teach you one first)

623
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:39,780
(Let me think first)

624
00:15:40,410 --> 00:15:41,310
Zhou

625
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:44,060
ran, ran, fell, ran, ran, fell, ran.

626
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:45,880
Did he fall or run?

627
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:47,560
Huh?

628
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:48,120
Wait.

629
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:48,840
Let me watch again.

630
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:49,520
How does this work?

631
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:50,680
(Let me get a closer look)
Do it again.

632
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:51,390
Watch carefully.

633
00:15:51,390 --> 00:15:52,060
(One more lesson)
Zhou

634
00:15:53,040 --> 00:15:54,200
ran, fell, ran, ran,

635
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:54,800
fell, ran,

636
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:56,320
fell, ran, ran.

637
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:57,320
Did he fall or run?

638
00:15:57,380 --> 00:15:59,240
(Not a freeze-frame)

639
00:15:59,240 --> 00:16:00,240
Ran.

640
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:02,480
I don't really know how
to play either.

641
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:04,480
I only half-remember it.

642
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:06,720
(Are you serious?)
What are you doing?

643
00:16:07,260 --> 00:16:08,040
(My bad)

644
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:09,320
Teach me a black-magic game.

645
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:11,160
(Teach me one)
You know black magic, right?

646
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:12,240
(I don't)
I don't.

647
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:13,120
(Shocked)
You don't know black magic?

648
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:13,560
Nope.

649
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:14,760
Then what are you going to do later?

650
00:16:14,760 --> 00:16:15,960
(Professor Zhou begins class)
Here's how black magic works.

651
00:16:16,920 --> 00:16:18,760
I turn around

652
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:19,680
so I can't see you

653
00:16:19,680 --> 00:16:21,880
pick something in the room.

654
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:23,320
You pick one thing,

655
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:24,480
(Listening carefully)
and then

656
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,520
when I turn back around,

657
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:26,080
you start asking,

658
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:27,600
and I'll know what you picked.

659
00:16:28,380 --> 00:16:29,060
(That's possible?)

660
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:29,970
What is it?

661
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:32,440
You need two people to play.

662
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:34,080
(Black magic takes teamwork)
One person secretly cues the other.

663
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:35,640
The other person starts checking,

664
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:36,200
one thing,

665
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:36,680
then another.

666
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:37,160
And the trick is,

667
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:39,120
the answer comes
right after something black.

668
00:16:39,780 --> 00:16:40,480
(It clicks)

669
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:41,000
Got it.

670
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,200
(I still don't get it)
Why black?

671
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:43,320
(Time to show what we learned)
Let's play a round.

672
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:44,990
Okay. Pick something.

673
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:46,400
(Pick what?)
How do I choose?

674
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:47,080
Anything you want.

675
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:49,400
Anything in this room.

676
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:50,240
Okay.

677
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:51,160
Done?

678
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:52,080
Now ask me.

679
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:53,320
Ask if she picked each thing,

680
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:55,000
and I'll say yes or no.

681
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:55,960
Yes or no?

682
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:56,760
Right. Just ask.

683
00:16:56,760 --> 00:16:57,600
Is it this?

684
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:58,440
Which one?

685
00:16:58,440 --> 00:16:59,400
Her.

686
00:16:59,400 --> 00:16:59,760
Her?

687
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:00,440
Her herself.

688
00:17:00,440 --> 00:17:00,960
The person.

689
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:02,000
No.

690
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:02,960
Is it you?

691
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:03,600
No.

692
00:17:03,860 --> 00:17:05,380
(Trying to understand)

693
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:07,070
Is it this?

694
00:17:07,070 --> 00:17:07,830
No.

695
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:10,520
Is it this?

696
00:17:10,620 --> 00:17:11,560
(The ceiling is black)

697
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:12,480
No.

698
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:13,640
Is it me?

699
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:14,110
Yes.

700
00:17:14,220 --> 00:17:15,700
(How did he know?)

701
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:16,590
Why?

702
00:17:16,590 --> 00:17:17,960
(Teach me, master)

703
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:19,070
You still don't get it?

704
00:17:19,100 --> 00:17:19,960
(What's the trick?)

705
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:21,070
Just now,

706
00:17:21,070 --> 00:17:22,960
he asked me about several things, right?

707
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:23,800
Then on the second-to-last one,

708
00:17:23,800 --> 00:17:24,680
he pointed

709
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:26,070
at something black.

710
00:17:26,070 --> 00:17:26,800
Once the black item came up,

711
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:27,280
he said no.

712
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:28,280
The next thing

713
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:29,080
is the answer.

714
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:31,000
The thing after the black item
is the answer.

715
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:31,320
Right.

716
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:32,960
So you need someone

717
00:17:32,960 --> 00:17:34,360
to secretly cue you.

718
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:36,960
(Got it now)
Okay, now I get it.

719
00:17:37,440 --> 00:17:38,360
What I was saying earlier is,

720
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:39,840
before you start,

721
00:17:39,840 --> 00:17:41,240
if you say "watch closely",

722
00:17:41,240 --> 00:17:42,920
then "fell"

723
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:43,840
is the secret rule too.

724
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:45,080
Same with Counting Horses?

725
00:17:45,080 --> 00:17:46,000
Like they all have some hidden rule.

726
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:48,960
Do you know the switch game?

727
00:17:49,450 --> 00:17:50,280
I've played it,

728
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:51,560
but I kinda forgot.

729
00:17:51,560 --> 00:17:52,680
(Need a memory reboot)
Run me through it.

730
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:54,280
(Switch game)
Okay. This is on. This is off.

731
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:55,000
This is on. This is off.

732
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:55,720
Is this on or off?

733
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:57,480
Off.

734
00:17:57,480 --> 00:17:58,280
Wrong.

735
00:17:58,700 --> 00:17:59,640
(That's wrong?)

736
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:00,600
That's off.

737
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:01,400
Nope.

738
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,360
Do you know it?

739
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:04,240
(I don't)
No. What's the rule?

740
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:05,440
If I tell you,

741
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:06,160
that ruins the fun.

742
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:08,280
This is on. This is off. On, off.

743
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:09,640
On, off.

744
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:10,760
Is this on or off?

745
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:15,600
Off.

746
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:16,960
Correct.

747
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:17,800
Now she gets it.

748
00:18:17,820 --> 00:18:19,040
(Completely lost)

749
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:21,000
Just watch if their mouth
is open or closed.

750
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:23,240
(Instantly gets it)
It's the final position of the mouth.

751
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:23,680
Exactly.

752
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:25,840
What was that butterfly-catching again?

753
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:26,760
Catch the Butterfly?

754
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:27,960
That one uses a 3x3 grid.

755
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:28,960
A 3x3 grid.

756
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:29,960
Counting Horses has a trick too.

757
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:31,160
That's based on a number.

758
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:33,280
Right. Before you start counting horses,

759
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:34,600
count the words in the sentence you say.

760
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:35,880
You know all of these?

761
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:37,160
I know... two of them.

762
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:38,420
(Only these two)

763
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:41,270
Those three are having way too much fun.

764
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:43,480
Are you guys done yet?

765
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:45,080
Hurry up!

766
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:47,160
We've played
every black-magic game we know.

767
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:51,520
Now, player Nan Do,
please come in alone.

768
00:18:53,610 --> 00:18:54,480
I'm here.

769
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:55,400
Hello, sir.

770
00:18:59,300 --> 00:19:00,940
(The Truth's masterpiece: Waiting)

771
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:02,980
(Round 3 Chemistry Test: Failed)

772
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,880
Let's make this one quick.

773
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:06,080
(Just start already)
Yeah. Let's just go.

774
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:06,640
Speedrun.

775
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:07,320
Speedrun?

776
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:07,800
Speedrun.

777
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:08,320
Go in.

778
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:09,160
(Suddenly fired up)
Okay, let's do it.

779
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:10,960
We'll show you what real chemistry is.

780
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:12,400
They still need time to set up props.

781
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:13,320
They need to think of questions too.

782
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:14,140
(Question bank loading...)

783
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:16,480
Heads or tails?

784
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:17,880
If it's heads or tails,
always pick heads.

785
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:18,320
Heads.

786
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:20,720
We really can't lock down these rules.

787
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:21,360
No, we can.

788
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:22,240
We almost won just now.

789
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:24,360
We nailed everything at the start.

790
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:25,600
I even got your question right.

791
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:26,640
What if they're deliberately

792
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:28,000
trying to make the last person fail?

793
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,160
(It won't be that easy)
They definitely are.

794
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:30,560
That last section is just harder.

795
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:31,520
Got to be it.

796
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:33,280
They're hearing every word I say.

797
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:34,080
It's fine. We...

798
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:35,920
Yeah, they're listening,

799
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:37,360
but that actually makes it harder

800
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:38,080
for them to come up with questions.

801
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:39,120
Right.

802
00:19:39,120 --> 00:19:40,060
(Classic Ning)

803
00:19:40,440 --> 00:19:41,040
Okay.

804
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:42,440
Let's settle on a real strategy.

805
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:44,560
From now on, small, soft, pretty,
and weak are equal to no.

806
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:46,040
(Strategy: deny everything)
Exactly.

807
00:19:46,040 --> 00:19:48,600
If they ask what someone ate
for breakfast,

808
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:49,320
nothing.

809
00:19:49,380 --> 00:19:50,240
(Chemistry notes)

810
00:19:50,240 --> 00:19:51,960
So, just say no to everything?

811
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:52,520
Yeah.

812
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:53,480
(The Truth Crash Course)
What music do they listen to?

813
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:53,880
None.

814
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:54,960
They don't listen to music.

815
00:19:54,960 --> 00:19:57,400
That's the idea. Perfect.

816
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,280
One more.

817
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:00,440
How often does he shower?

818
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:01,240
Never.

819
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:02,100
(In unison)

820
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:03,480
Exactly. That's the idea.

821
00:20:03,480 --> 00:20:04,520
(Addicted to the quiz)
One more.

822
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:05,440
No more questions.

823
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:07,000
That's enough.

824
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:08,280
Getting hooked on it, huh?

825
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:11,200
Like, is Jin Pretty a girl?

826
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,200
No.

827
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:14,000
(We're going that far?)
Seriously?

828
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:14,720
For real?

829
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:17,440
All right. Challenge accepted. Let's go.

830
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:19,440
Hurry up.

831
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:21,160
(Victory feels guaranteed)
We're clearing it this time.

832
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:22,440
Now,

833
00:20:22,440 --> 00:20:25,040
player Ding Dang, come in alone.

834
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:26,360
Left hand.

835
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:27,240
He doesn't matter.

836
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:29,440
You all know black magic, right?

837
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:30,680
Ning, do you know it?

838
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:31,680
Ning probably does too.

839
00:20:31,680 --> 00:20:32,840
(I don't)
I actually don't.

840
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:34,160
We'll show you.

841
00:20:34,680 --> 00:20:35,400
(I'll work with you)
I'll do it.

842
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:36,000
Right.

843
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:36,520
You do it.

844
00:20:36,520 --> 00:20:37,080
Come on.

845
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:38,400
I mean,
the three of us can do it together.

846
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:39,320
It takes three people.

847
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:39,840
It's a three-person game.

848
00:20:39,840 --> 00:20:41,240
(Fine, I'll play along)
How does the three-person version work?

